    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen writing treesitter queries in the query editor opened by `:EditQuery` (or `vim.treesitter.query.edit()`), is it supposed to apply the highlights related to the standard captures in these queries in the source buffer?\n\nE.g. given the following query:\n```scm\n((sym_lit) @comment\n (#eq? @comment \"comment\"))\n```\n\nWhen I hover over `@comment`, all the relevant matching nodes are highlighted in the source buffer (the one we opened `:EditQuery` from) as expected with hl-DiagnosticVirtualTextHint, but the relevant `@comment` highlights are not applied. If I copy this treesitter query and save it to `$rtp/queries/<lang>/highlights.scm`, restart neovim and reopen the buffer, the comment highlights are applied to the `@comment` treesitter nodes as expected.\n\nSo is `:EditQuery` buffer only for viewing what nodes match a query? Wouldn't it be more useful if it applied the relevant standard capture highlights too to the source buffer for a more interactive treesitter query development?\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.12.4",
